cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its data artifacts, please cite the repository.
  If you use the findings, cite the paper listed under preferred-citation.
title: >-
  kalshi-makers-takers-persistence: replication and persistence analysis of the
  Kalshi prediction market
abstract: >-
  A read-only research instrument that reproduces Bürgi, Deng and Whelan's
  analysis of the Kalshi prediction market over their own window (2021 to April
  2025) from independently collected public API data, then extends it past two
  dated treatments they could not observe: the maker fee and the paper's own
  publication. Ships a machine-readable reconstruction of Kalshi's fee schedule
  from sixteen dated captures of the exchange's published document, a versioned
  category mapping, and an analysis plan committed before any extension estimate
  was computed.
type: software
